.TH SUNSHINE-STREAM-PREP 1 "2026-10-10" "sunshine-stream-prep" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sunshine-stream-prep \- set the display mode for a Sunshine stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sunshine-stream-prep
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sunshine-stream-prep
sets output
.B DP\-2
to the best mode matching the Sunshine client resolution via
.BR kscreen-doctor (1),
then polls up to 30 seconds for the mode to apply.
.P
Takes no arguments. Target size comes from the Sunshine client environment
(width/height/fps), defaulting to 2560x1440@240. Mode choice prefers an exact
WxH match, else the closest aspect ratio, then the highest refresh at or below
the target.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I SUNSHINE_CLIENT_WIDTH
Desired width. Default: 2560.
.TP
.I SUNSHINE_CLIENT_HEIGHT
Desired height. Default: 1440.
.TP
.I SUNSHINE_CLIENT_FPS
Desired refresh. Default: 240.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sunshine pre-stream hook:
.IP
.EX
sunshine-stream-prep
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Target mode applied.
.TP
.B 1
Mode did not apply within 30 s, or output not found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sunshine-stream-undo (1),
.BR sunshine-gamescope-run (1),
.BR kscreen-doctor (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
